# Copy to .dev.vars for local dev. Never put real values in THIS file:
# it is committed. The Worker reads these, the browser never does.
# The hosted Meta key (the older name META_MODEL_API_KEY still works). Only worker/modelBackend.ts reads it, and only for a capability whose
# backend is "hosted" (see the model switch below). A child-facing deployment on our own models can leave it empty.
MODEL_API_KEY=
META_MODEL_API_URL=https://api.meta.ai/v1
MUREKA_API_KEY=
# Theme songs (worker/themeSong.ts): a name and a sung song for a build, written by the text model and sung by Mureka. OFF unless this is exactly "on".
# Each song costs one text-model call and about $0.04 at Mureka (measured 2026-11-03). It is METERED: 5 new songs a week per device (a grown-up can lower it or switch songs off),
# and SONG_MONTHLY_BUDGET songs a month across everyone, kept in D1 (shared/songQuota.ts, worker/songStore.ts). Metering needs the D1 binding; SONG_MONTHLY_BUDGET unset means
# NO song is made (fails closed). An R2 bucket bound as UPLOADS (toyventor-uploads, bound in wrangler.jsonc) keeps finished songs past Mureka's 30-day link (optional; see docs/product/deploy-checklist.md).
THEME_SONG=
SONG_MONTHLY_BUDGET=
# THEME_SONG_QUOTA=off runs the route UNMETERED for local probes only (no D1, no device id): never set it in production. THEME_SONG_MAX_STARTS caps songs per Worker instance when set.
THEME_SONG_QUOTA=
THEME_SONG_MAX_STARTS=
# Optional: model id for Create mode (/api/muse/spark). Empty means the
# default in worker/muse.ts.
MUSE_SPARK_MODEL=
# Optional: the opt-in "Smart face" for the Kip selfie (/api/selfie/face-parts finds eyes and mouth with SAM 3.1,
# /api/selfie/cartoon redraws the photo with Muse Image). It sends ONE downscaled photo of the child to Meta's models, so:
#   - it is OFF unless this is exactly "on" and the hosted segment capability is configured (MODEL_API_KEY set and SEGMENT_BACKEND not self/off:
#     SAM has no adapter for our own models yet, so "self" means off);
#   - every request also needs the parent gate (x-parent-proof, needs the D1 binding and PARENT_GATE_SECRET or the seeded key)
#     and the client's consent screen (x-selfie-consent: v1);
#   - keep it OFF in production until the COPPA review is done.
SELFIE_CLOUD=

# Model switch (worker/modelBackend.ts, docs/decisions/0008-meta-models-and-under-18-users.md). Server-side only; a client can never choose.
# MODEL_BACKEND = hosted | self | off. Unset means hosted (today's behaviour). "self" NEVER falls back to hosted: with no endpoint below it is off.
# A capability's own variable wins over MODEL_BACKEND: TEXT_BACKEND, SEGMENT_BACKEND, IMAGE_BACKEND, TRANSCRIBE_BACKEND.
MODEL_BACKEND=
TEXT_BACKEND=
SEGMENT_BACKEND=
IMAGE_BACKEND=
TRANSCRIBE_BACKEND=
# Our own models: https base URL (http only on localhost), optional key. Text also needs the served model name; SELF_TEXT_API is
# "responses" (default) or "chat" (/chat/completions; llama.cpp serves Glimmer on this one). SELF_TEXT_REASONING is Glimmer's reasoning
# strength, sent in the system prompt: low (default), medium, high, xhigh. Do NOT set it to off or leave the line out: with no line Glimmer thinks about 4 times as long
# (measured 2026-11-04: 3,600 to 4,000 tokens and 44 to 48 s per make call, against 800 to 1,100 tokens and 10 to 14 s with low).
# Glimmer v1 on Modal (scripts/modal/glimmer_server.py), with MODEL_BACKEND=self (or TEXT_BACKEND=self for the text capability only):
#   SELF_TEXT_URL=https://<workspace>--toyventor-glimmer.us-east.modal.run/v1   SELF_TEXT_MODEL=muse-glimmer-30B   SELF_TEXT_API=chat
#   SELF_TEXT_KEY = the key you gave the Modal secret glimmer-api-key (LLAMA_API_KEY). Segment and image have no adapter yet.
SELF_TEXT_URL=
SELF_TEXT_KEY=
SELF_TEXT_MODEL=
SELF_TEXT_API=
SELF_TEXT_REASONING=
# "tuned" sends the SHORT prompt (shared/forgeTunePrompt.ts) to a model trained on it (scripts/tuning/README.md). Leave empty for the base Glimmer: it needs the long prompt.
SELF_TEXT_PROMPT=
# MAKE-FROM-WORDS runs on OUR OWN models by default (docs/specs/forge-ai-spec.md, "Fast path"): the tuned model first for a hat or head wish (SELF_FAST_*), our own base Glimmer (SELF_TEXT_* above, with
# SELF_TEXT_API=chat) as the fallback and the repairer. The hosted model is never used for make, and there is no setting for it. Local development with only a hosted key needs FORGE_AUDIENCE_DEFAULT=adult.
# SELF_FAST_URL is an https address (/v1 included), SELF_FAST_MODEL the served name (forge-glimmer), SELF_FAST_KEY the key that server takes. The tuned model is on whenever URL and model are set;
# FORGE_FAST_MODE=off (exactly) is the kill switch.
FORGE_FAST_MODE=
SELF_FAST_URL=
SELF_FAST_KEY=
SELF_FAST_MODEL=
# The OPERATOR's safety net, not a user option: FORGE_AUDIENCE_DEFAULT=adult lets the hosted model answer make-from-words as the fallback and repairer (for example while the Modal servers are cold).
# FORGE_HOSTED_FOR_ADULTS=off (exactly) beats it and keeps make on our own models only. Unset = our own models only.
FORGE_HOSTED_FOR_ADULTS=
FORGE_AUDIENCE_DEFAULT=
# The grown-up gate in front of the routes that use ANOTHER model (docs/specs/forge-ai-spec.md, "Parent supervision"): on only when set to exactly "on". OFF = today's behaviour.
# A proof at most 3 minutes old for segment (SAM outline, camera pick-up), image (art, skins) and transcribe; 5 minutes for AR (the Scavenger camera, request purpose "ar").
PARENT_GATE_SEGMENT=
PARENT_GATE_IMAGE=
PARENT_GATE_TRANSCRIBE=
PARENT_GATE_AR=
SELF_SEGMENT_URL=
SELF_SEGMENT_KEY=
SELF_IMAGE_URL=
SELF_IMAGE_KEY=
# Voice input for Describe & build (worker/transcribe.ts, POST/GET /api/transcribe). Two ways, and nothing else turns it on (an unset switch, MODEL_BACKEND=hosted, a missing key or
# address all leave it off, and the microphone button stays hidden):
#   TRANSCRIBE_BACKEND=hosted  Meta's muse-voice-transcribe-1.0 with MODEL_API_KEY. A DEMO-ONLY exception (Dan, 2026-11-04, docs/decisions/0008): it must be written out exactly like this
#                              (the master MODEL_BACKEND never enables it), and the page sends a 16 kHz mono WAV. Remove the line to end it.
# There is no child-facing voice route yet: a self-hosted speech model has not been chosen.

# Text to part (worker/forgeMake.ts, worker/forgeOptimizer.ts). The optimizer daemon is what builds and checks the part; with no URL the routes
# answer 503 "disabled". A non-loopback daemon MUST also have a token. Local dev: http://127.0.0.1:8791 (npm run forge:optimizer).
FORGE_OPTIMIZER_URL=
FORGE_OPTIMIZER_TOKEN=
# "1" puts the grown-up proof back in front of making and previewing a part. Unset: making needs only the device id and the rate limits;
# printing and saving the file always need the proof.
FORGE_MAKE_REQUIRES_PROOF=
# Signs the spoken names, so /api/voice only says what this Worker produced. At least 16 characters. Deployed: `wrangler secret put VOICE_SIGNING_KEY`.
VOICE_SIGNING_KEY=

# The grown-up check (worker/parent.ts). Signs the challenge and proof tokens. Unset: a random secret kept in the database is used.
# The Meta model key is no longer a fallback for this (2026-11-03), so a deployment with no model key still has a working gate.
PARENT_GATE_SECRET=
